# Planning artifacts (this repo)

## Plan first (UiPlan)

For non-trivial work (3+ steps, multiple files, unclear scope, or when
`UIPATH_PLAN_GATE=1`), load `.cursor/skills/uiplan/SKILL.md` **before** touching
build tools. Default path: `uipath_plan_ground` -> `uipath_plan_spec_new` ->
`uipath_plan_plan_new` -> `uipath_plan_tasks_new` -> `uipath_plan_review` ->
`uipath_plan_accept` -> (later) `uipath_plan_publish`. Optional one-shot:
`uipath_plan_uiplan_new`.

Legacy single-file only when explicitly requested: `uipath_plan_brainstorm` ->
`uipath_plan_new` -> `uipath_plan_refine` -> accept -> publish. Do not use
`uipath_plan_refine` on UiPlan **folder** drafts.

## Drafts vs published

- **UiPlan drafts** live under `.cursor/plans/<YYYY-MM-DD-slug>/` with
  `spec.md`, `plan.md`, `tasks.md`, `.meta.yaml` — edit those files or re-run
  MCP stages; do not use `uipath_plan_refine` on this layout.
- **Legacy single-file drafts** live under `.cursor/plans/<YYYY-MM-DD-slug>.md`
  (git-ignored, per-user). Created by `uipath_plan_new`; prefer
  `uipath_plan_refine` so validation + snapshots kick in.
- **Published plans** live under `docs/plans/` (git-tracked). Promote via
  `uipath_plan_publish`; the plan must have `status: accepted` first.

## Authoring rules

- File shape: `.cursor/skills/writing-uipath-plans/SKILL.md` +
  `docs/plans/_TEMPLATE.md` (front matter with `slug / title / date /
  status / owner / project_type`, plus `accepted_at / accepted_by /
  rejection_reason / published_at`).
- Diagrams: `.cursor/skills/mermaid-diagram-builder/SKILL.md` (tinted
  fills, `classDef`, `linkStyle`; no inline `style` fills).
- `uipath_plan_refine` and `uipath_plan_save` refuse plans without at
  least one ```mermaid block.
- Prefer the plan MCP tools over raw reads/writes: `uipath_plan_list`
  (`scope=drafts|published|both`), `uipath_plan_read`,
  `uipath_plan_render_mermaid`, `uipath_plan_status_set`.

## Acceptance gate

- `uipath_plan_accept` stamps the draft; `uipath_plan_reject` refuses
  empty reasons.
- When `UIPATH_PLAN_GATE=1`, `uipath_workflow_write_file` /
  `_install_package` / `_deploy` / `_publish` all require an accepted
  plan. Complements `UIPATH_DESIGN_APPROVAL_ENABLED`.
- `uipath_plan_status_set` to `done` still requires an approved design
  when the design gate is on.

## After editing plans

Run `python scripts/generate_plan_index.py` (or rely on
`uipath_plan_save` / `uipath_plan_publish` which trigger the same
script). Formal PDD/SDD/ADD lifecycle: `docs/PDD_LIFECYCLE.md` — link
paths via plan front matter `linked_pdd` when applicable.
